			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync Element submodule with Mountain, Sky, and Cocoon changes\n\nRoutine submodule synchronization bringing in latest changes across the application stack:\n\n1. Mountain:\n   - Add LRU cache for FindFilesInWorkspace with 2.5s TTL and 128-entry capacity to reduce latency during fuzzy file matching (Cmd+P typing bursts)\n   - Gate dev_log! macro on cfg!(debug_assertions) to eliminate logging overhead in release builds via LLVM dead-code-elimination\n   - Revert verbose development naming back to simple \"Mountain\" for binary, lib, identifier, and productName\n   - Remove obsolete .Backup files\n\n2. Sky:\n   - Fix tree view data provider attachment for late-registering extensions (gitlens, clangd, dependencies)\n   - Replace fixed 5-retry × 150ms schedule with exponential backoff (~10s across 12 retries)\n   - Add PendingAttaches set to queue views that exhaust retry budget\n   - Add RetryPendingAttaches() to sweep pending views when successful attach indicates workbench bridge is wired\n\n3. Cocoon:\n   - Regenerate route manifest timestamp from 2026-04-25T01:20:57Z to 2026-04-25T01:28:02Z, no functional changes\n\nImpact: Mountain's file search is now optimized for rapid Cmd+P interactions with LRU caching. Release builds eliminate dev_log overhead. Sky now handles extensions that register views 3-5 seconds into boot. Extension host updated to latest.",
